{
	"name": "Bi-way: route customer replies to the team inbox",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "### How it works\nHelps teams that answer customers from their usual mailboxes. Every message a customer sends to your Bi-way numbers or RCS agent starts the workflow. Button taps are skipped, since the workflow that sent the buttons handles them. Typed messages are routed by keywords, in French and English, to billing, delivery or customer service for the rest. The chosen mailbox receives an email with the sender, the number, the channel, the date and the message.\n\n**Limits:** Answering the email does not reach the customer: reply from Bi-way. Bi-way sends each received message to every workflow listening, so typed answers meant for another workflow, such as YES or a rating, are emailed too. Bi-way does not send an event again if your n8n cannot be reached.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **Bi-way** community node (`n8n-nodes-biway-messenger`, [instructions](https://github.com/pocket-communication/n8n-nodes-biway-messenger#installation)). Tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.45.4 and n8n Cloud 3.1.0.\n2. Create a **Bi-Way API** credential with an API key from Bi-way › Settings › Security.\n3. Add an SMTP credential and replace `n8n@example.com`, `billing@example.com`, `delivery@example.com` and `support@example.com` with your addresses.\n4. Your n8n must be reachable over HTTPS. Publish the workflow: the trigger registers its webhook by itself.\n5. Send a message containing the word `invoice` to your Bi-way number, then check the billing mailbox.\n\n### Customization\nAdapt the keywords in **Route by keywords**, or add an output and an email node for another team. To keep typed answers out, extend the condition of **Only typed messages**.",
				"height": 590,
				"width": 620
			},
